Name is misleading here, this isn't actually a persisted status. These are more like human-friendly named filters which map to different queries:

```rb
scope :popped, -> { joins(:pop) }
scope :active, -> { where.missing(:pop) }
scope :unassigned, -> { where.missing :assignments }
```

I wanna let things cook for a bit before we pour concrete here, see what other filters we'll need and what's the common theme.

