`removeEventListener` will not remove the listeners here because `.bind(this)` creates a new function each time. Store the bound handler(s) on the instance (e.g., `this.beforeUnloadHandler = this.handleBeforeUnload.bind(this)`) and use the same references for both `addEventListener` and `removeEventListener`.
```suggestion
    if (!this._beforeUnloadHandler) {
      this._beforeUnloadHandler = this.handleBeforeUnload.bind(this)
    }
    if (!this._beforeVisitHandler) {
      this._beforeVisitHandler = this.handleBeforeVisit.bind(this)
    }

    window.addEventListener("beforeunload", this._beforeUnloadHandler)
    window.addEventListener("turbo:before-visit", this._beforeVisitHandler)
  }

  disconnect() {
    if (this._beforeUnloadHandler) {
      window.removeEventListener("beforeunload", this._beforeUnloadHandler)
    }
    if (this._beforeVisitHandler) {
      window.removeEventListener("turbo:before-visit", this._beforeVisitHandler)
    }
```

Same issue as in `form_controller`: the bound function references differ between `addEventListener` and `removeEventListener`, so listeners will accumulate across connections. Persist the bound callbacks on the controller instance and remove using those stored references.
```suggestion
  constructor(...args) {
    super(...args)
    this.handleBeforeUnloadCallback = this.handleBeforeUnload.bind(this)
    this.handleBeforeVisitCallback = this.handleBeforeVisit.bind(this)
  }

  connect() {
    window.addEventListener("beforeunload", this.handleBeforeUnloadCallback)
    window.addEventListener("turbo:before-visit", this.handleBeforeVisitCallback)
  }

  disconnect() {
    window.removeEventListener("beforeunload", this.handleBeforeUnloadCallback)
    window.removeEventListener("turbo:before-visit", this.handleBeforeVisitCallback)
```

On mobile this raises the entire `.cards__new-column` container above neighboring columns even when the dialog is closed, which can increase the clickable/overlay area over adjacent cards. To minimize unintended layering changes, consider applying the z-index only when the `<dialog>` is open (there’s an established pattern in this file using `:has(dialog[open])` for similar UI).
```suggestion

      &:has(dialog[open]) {
        z-index: 2;
      }
```

`btn--ensure-tap-target-size` enlarges the hit area via an absolutely positioned `::before` without increasing the element’s layout box. In `.card__tags` (a tight `display:flex` row with a small `gap`), this expanded hit area is very likely to overlap adjacent tag links and steal taps. Consider enforcing the minimum 44px size via `min-inline-size`/`min-block-size` (and centering contents) or otherwise reserving space (e.g., extra margin/gap for the trigger) so neighboring controls remain tappable.
```suggestion
      --tap-target-min-size: 44px;

      min-block-size: var(--tap-target-min-size);
      min-inline-size: var(--tap-target-min-size);
      justify-content: center;
```

